## Game complete — final verification

**Summary:** Playable ThreeJS FPS prototype verified end-to-end. Entry HTML at \`./index.html\` (ThreeJS 0.185.1 CDN, 148 lines). Gameplay: click-to-lock pointer look, WASD + shift sprint, hitscan rifle with recoil/spread/tracer/muzzle flash, R reload, wave-spawning enemy bots with chase/attack AI, HP/ammo/wave/kill HUD, procedural WebAudio gunshots and hit blips.

**Public game link:** https://indianapolis-highlight-allowing-dna.trycloudflare.com

**Final commit:** https://github.com/AgentsLoop/PlayGround/commit/${SHA}

**Deployment and test status:**
- Local: tmux session \`app-server\`, \`python3 -m http.server 3000\`, port 3000 HTTP 200 serving \`./index.html\` — RUNNING/PASS.
- Public URL: HTTP 200, serves identical \`index.html\` (title + HUD verified) — PASS.
- Browser test (chromium headless + SwiftShader, 1280x720, against public URL): PASS — overlay card, HUD (controls/wave/kills, HP, ammo), 3D arena and bots render; screenshots below are from the public URL session.
- JS syntax (\`node --check\` on inline module): PASS.

**Known limitations:** Greybox systems demo, not COD visual parity: procedural boxes only, no scanned 4K PBR, no GI/volumetrics, no mocap hands/animation, no multiplayer/netcode/anticheat, no persistent decals/destruction. Full AAA parity remains blocked (studio-scale assets, team, budget).

